# What the generator rendered for every `commands/*.md` page before the standing text of `commands.py`,
# `add_commands.py`, `pin_commands.py`, `ground_command.py` and `sail_section.py` moved out of their string
# literals and into `assets/toolkit/commands/`, as SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of each generated file.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured at 074aa35, the commit this change was written on
# top of, and the new path has to reproduce them exactly (`tests/test_command_pages.py`). Anyone can take
# the same reading: check out 074aa35, copy `tests/command_pages.py` from this branch over it, and run
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 tests/command_pages.py
#
# Eight projects, because these pages branch on more than one thing at once and a record taken at one
# would pass with half the branches stubbed out: the profile, a service that keeps its events and one that
# does not, a browser app and none, no application at all, a managed destination and none, both layouts,
# and an adopted repository with candidates outstanding beside one with none. `tests/command_pages.py`
# names each and says what it reaches.
#
# Every page a project receives from those five modules is here, and so are the ones they only assemble —
# `cruise.md`, `benchmark.md`, `mutation.md` and the rest come from modules this slice does not touch, and
# a row of theirs that moved is this slice having disturbed something it was not moving.
#
# A deliberate edit to a page changes these, which is the point: the line a reviewer has to see change is
# in this file, beside the diff that changed it.
#
#
# Re-taken for the scheduling rules — two bands, a state per slice, refill at every boundary, a `question`
# deck-log kind (`changelog.d/sail-scheduling-is-a-state.md`). Only the rows named there moved:
# `commands/cruise.md`, `commands/sail.md`, `commands/where-are-we.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the review cadence — once per slice over the whole diff, a return spot-checked and never
# reviewed (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-review-once-per-slice.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the committed return — a shipwright hands back `commit <hash>` or `no commit`, and the session
# integrates the commit (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-a-return-is-a-commit.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `commands/sail.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
